NOTE ON COMPONENT LICENCES

This repository's own code is MIT-licensed. Individual neural components it
integrates (ECAPA-TDNN, WavLM, F5-TTS, Llama-3, etc.) carry their own
licences. See docs/licensing_audit.md for the per-component commercial-safety
posture. In particular:

  * F5-TTS released weights are CC-BY-NC (non-commercial). The code path is
    shipped; commercial use requires a permissively-licensed replacement
    checkpoint or retraining on owned data.
  * eSpeak-ng / phonemizer are GPL-3.0. The pipeline replaces these by design
    with a permissively-licensed Indic articulatory ruleset for any commercial
    build, so the front end ships without copyleft exposure.
  * VoxCeleb-trained speaker encoders (ECAPA-TDNN) inherit the dataset's
    research-only terms; commercial deployment may require retraining on
    consented data.

Verify the licence of every checkpoint against its actual LICENSE file before
commercial use. Code licence and weights licence frequently differ; the
weights licence is the binding term.
